.TH SDL_ReadAsyncIO 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ReadAsyncIO \- Start an async read.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_ReadAsyncIO(SDL_AsyncIO *asyncio, void *ptr, Uint64 offset, Uint64 size, SDL_AsyncIOQueue *queue, void *userdata);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function reads up to
.BR size
bytes from
.BR offset
position in the data source to the area pointed at by
.BR ptr \[char46]
This function may read less bytes than requested\[char46]
.PP
This function returns as quickly as possible; it does not wait for the read to complete\[char46] On a successful return, this work will continue in the background\[char46] If the work begins, even failure is asynchronous: a failing return value from this function only means the work couldn\(aqt start at all\[char46]
.PP
.BR ptr
must remain available until the work is done, and may be accessed by the system at any time until then\[char46] Do not allocate it on the stack, as this might take longer than the life of the calling function to complete!
.PP
An
.BR SDL_AsyncIOQueue
must be specified\[char46] The newly-created task will be added to it when it completes its work\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I asyncio
a pointer to an
.BR SDL_AsyncIO
structure\[char46]
.TP
.I ptr
a pointer to a buffer to read data into\[char46]
.TP
.I offset
the position to start reading in the data source\[char46]
.TP
.I size
the number of bytes to read from the data source\[char46]
.TP
.I queue
a queue to add the new
.BR SDL_AsyncIO
to\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
an app-defined pointer that will be provided with the task results\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_WriteAsyncIO (3),
